codex
I found the cause of the long entry-only run: the end-to-end claim is intentionally dependent on the loop claim as a circularity, so deleting the loop claim from the module removes its proof dependency and causes unbounded symbolic unrolling. I’m stopping that non-equivalent isolation probe and will instead select each labeled target from one module that retains both claims, preserving the helper dependency while still running each target independently.
